    "titulo": "Travel: airport, train, hotel",
    "objetivo": "Buy a train ticket and ask about platforms and delays, handle check-in and luggage at the airport, book a hotel room, and describe a short trip in the past. Use «da» for where a train leaves from and «per» for where a ticket goes, say «in ritardo» for a delay, and choose «essere» or «avere» in the passato prossimo. Avoid the English-speaker traps: «tardi» for a late train, «a» for the destination of a ticket, and «avere» with verbs of movement.",
